# The Colo config bundle's allowlist (G1-03). deploy/genesis/build-config-bundle.sh packs exactly these files, one repo
# path per line; `#` lines and blank lines are comments. A test (deploy/test/genesis-config-bundle.test.ts) compares
# the archive's names with the paths here, so adding a file means adding its line here in the same change.
#
# Groups: the compose files merged by deploy/common.sh (colo.yml, nats-auth.yml) and the overlays the deploy scripts
# merge (colo-public.yml, colo-notice.yml) or that run with colo (colo-kino.yml), and the files they mount; the shard
# files the services read; the BlueMap, Chunky and CoreProtect config and lock files the deploy checks; the SQL
# migrations colo-cd refreshes; the deploy scripts, their overlay, the release template and the Caddy snippets; and
# this build's own script and list.
#
# Never listed: secrets (compose/secrets/, deploy/test/ and everything under a state directory), *.env, *.pem,
# nats-auth.conf and node.env. The built plugin jars are not in git (plugin/*/build); the node pulls them through the
# lock files. The CoreProtect config template does not exist yet; see docs/runbooks/node-only-config.md.
